Chapters is an open-source, self-hostable "second brain" / team knowledge platform: markdown+YAML notes (Google OKF format), a live-preview editor, an AI-navigable knowledge graph (Graphify-inspired), real-time collaboration, and permission-scoped MCP access for AI assistants.

**Why:** started as the user's personal "which PKM tool" question, escalated into a full internal-tool-that's-also-OSS build for their company (PIIIX), which mostly does open-source projects. Full origin story and design rationale is in the repo's own README.

**Repo:** github.com/PIIIX-org/chapters (org-owned, not personal account — deliberate choice so it's not tied to the user's personal GitHub). Local clone at `~/Documents/chapters`. Renamed from "second-brain"/"Second Brain" to "Chapters" on 2026-07-15.

**Workflow established for this project:**
- Structure/research only — no code written yet, by explicit repeated instruction. Every design decision goes through: clarifying Q&A → present design → user confirms → write spec to `docs/superpowers/specs/YYYY-MM-DD-<topic>-design.md` → commit.
- Every substantive change goes: feature branch → commit → `gh pr create` → merge. Note: auto-merging a self-authored PR without human review has been blocked by the harness before (2026-07-15) — open the PR and let the user merge, don't attempt `gh pr merge` proactively.
- See [[chapters-readme-workflow]] — README.md must be updated to reflect every meaningful change, same PR as the change itself.

**State as of 2026-07-15:**
- All 6 sub-project specs written and merged: Auth & Vault/Sharing, Editor, Graph engine & view, Search, Real-time collaboration, MCP integration.
- A full security audit pass hardened all 6 specs (27 findings, critical→low) — see `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-12-security-audit-findings.md`.
- 8 user-flow/system diagrams added under `docs/superpowers/specs/diagrams/` (built with the `diagram-design` skill), covering onboarding, sharing, MCP connection, live collaboration, graph exploration, search, system architecture, and AI navigation.
- Known tracked-but-unspecced gaps: data export/portability (sub-project 7 candidate), notifications/activity feed, admin dashboard, MFA — listed in README's "Known gaps" section.
- Next likely phase: either sub-project 7 (data export) or moving toward an actual implementation plan/tech stack decision (Python + FastAPI + PostgreSQL was picked in an earlier abandoned attempt at writing-plans, before the user redirected back to research-only — that stack choice was never really settled as final).
